<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central Europe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> is the region between Western and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-europe">Eastern Europe</a>, broadly including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, the Czech lands, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> its western parts lay within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. In the modern era much of it was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> basin until 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-europe.jpg" alt="Central Europe" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grossgliederung_Europas.svg: NordNordWest derivative work: Dch (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grossgliederung_Europas-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
